    "explanation": "Rider, you get the full SGD 3.20 back. Driver, this is a billing-integrity correction of a phantom charge line — it is not a finding against your driving, and no distance or time money moves against you.\n\nThe disputed charge is a single SGD 3.20 ERP line for the 'Bukit Merah Central westbound' gantry, charged at 2026-09-21T11:43. That gantry carries coordinates (lat 1.3400, lng 103.7800), and on this trace — 169 fixes, 10-second sampling, coverage_pct 100, no gaps — the closest the vehicle ever came to it was 7,482.07 m, at fix index 65 (2026-09-21T11:40:50). POL-RD-09 matches a gantry to the trace by treating any fix within 250 m as a crossing. Nothing comes within 7 km, so the vehicle never passed this gantry. Under POL-RD-09(4) a charge line for a gantry the trace never passes is a billing-integrity failure; it is refunded in full as a standalone correction, available whether or not a deviation exists. That is the whole SGD 3.20.\n\nThe upfront fare itself is left as it is. fare_breakdown.fare_model is UPFRONT_QUOTE with quoted_fare_sgd 22.00 and charged_total 25.20 (base_fare 3.80 + distance_fare 10.00 + time_fare 7.40 + platform_fee 0.80 + tolls_erp 3.20). The only amount by which the charge exceeds the quote is 25.20 − 22.00 = 3.20, and that 3.20 is exactly this ERP line — nothing else is properly chargeable as a pass-through, since optimal_route_erp_sgd is 0.00 and the gantry is flagged on_optimal_route=false. Under POL-RD-11 the distance and time charges on an upfront-quoted trip were fixed at booking and POL-RD-02 does not run, so the trace's excess — 16.0 km actual against 12.5 km optimal, an excess of 3.5 km or 28%, which does clear POL-RD-01's 0.8 km and 20% gates — earns no distance or time refund. Because the amount returned equals the whole contested amount, the outcome is FULL_REFUND.\n\nOn your side, driver: the excess is not a MATERIAL deviation (3.5 km is below the 8.0 km gate and 28% below the 50% gate), so the POL-RD-06 driver_profile check is not engaged, no FULL_REFUND uplift of charged_total is available, and no driver-conduct referral follows from this trip's route. The profile is clean in any event: deviation_flags_90d is 0 against completed_trips_90d of 610, below both the count and ratio limbs. No exculpatory clause rescues the excess either: the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-09114-01 carries a null payload, so no advisory names any road the optimal route uses (POL-RD-03); the sole chat message is the rider's post-trip fare query, waypoint_hint is null and no road is named, so the POL-RD-04 corroboration test cannot be run and that clause is unavailable on the record; and neither pickup_amended_at nor dropoff_amended_at is set and amended_optimal_distance_km is null, so POL-RD-05 cannot be run. None of this costs you anything, because POL-RD-11 closes the distance-refund route on this trip regardless.\n\nThe rider's POL-RD-07 point — that the counterparty statement concedes the gantry was not seen or passed — is noted but not needed. The trace is unimpaired under POL-RD-07(a) to (c) (no gap over 90 s, no jump over 500 m, sampling interval 10 s), so no independent corroboration is required and POL-RD-09(4) reads the trace directly.\n\nNo escalation trigger fires. The trip identifiers match across trip_record, gps_trace and fare_breakdown (TRP-09114 throughout); the timestamps agree; the trace is not impaired; the refund is 3.20, far below both the SGD 150.00 ceiling and charged_total; and the one charge line with no counterpart in the trace is the very line refunded under POL-RD-09(4), which POL-RD-10(8) expressly excepts from escalation.\n\nConfidence: the deciding fact — that the charged gantry was never crossed — is carried by the gps_trace (nearest fix 7,482.07 m) and by the fare_breakdown (the gantry's own coordinates and its on_optimal_route=false flag), two independent artifacts both at full weight 1.0, so the cap is 1.0. Confidence is set at 0.95."
